                      <DistributedParameter id="itvMylzs8EG6JVBrrx7wng" name="Gastric emptying time" description="The time at which the (1-1/e)th part (approximately 63%) of the applied dose (fasted state) is released from the stomach into the duodenum according to a first order process. Please note that in the case that a meal is co-administered with the drug, the gastric emptying rate is described using a Weibull function. The parameters of the Weibull function and, thus, the gastric emptying time, then depend on the volume and composition of the meal" persistable="0" isFixedValue="0" dim="Time" quantityType="Parameter" negativeValuesAllowed="1" formula="7fyfbrwkh0S_tbTg_f4cYA" mode="Logical" isDefault="1" displayUnit="h">
